 "transients": {},
 "why": "On a copper layer of one slab (up to 105 um) the FEM put the power of a part as a volumetric source in that slab; one linear element through the copper carries half of such a load at its bottom node, so the surface minus column term read about half of q t / 2k. The part now enters through the outer face on every outer layer, as on thick copper: the surface of the FEM moves by up to the whole term, the column by a fraction of a milli-kelvin to a few milli-kelvin on the harness boards."
}
